                                   } src/mmain/resources/result
spring.mvc.view.suffix=.jsp


Advantages of View Resolver
The advantages of View Resolver in Spring MVC include:
Flexibility: View Resolver allows multiple view technologies to coexist in the same application, enabling developers to choose the most suitable technology for their specific needs. 
3
Loose Coupling: View Resolver provides a loose coupling between the controller and the view component, allowing for easier replacement of view technologies in the future. 
1
Performance: View resolvers can cache views, which improves performance by reducing the overhead of resolving views on every request. 
1
Configuration Flexibility: View Resolver can be configured to handle different types of views, such as JSPs for some views and Thymeleaf for others. 
1
Cache Management: View resolvers can cache view instances, which can be turned off by setting the cache property to false. 
1

These advantages make View Resolver a powerful tool in Spring MVC, enhancing the flexibility and performance of web applications

